            bluez, rfkill, python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi
Suggests: opensc-pkcs11, softhsm2
Description: BitLocker Network Unlock (MS-NKPU) server with PKCS#11 key backend
 JNKPU answers BitLocker Network Unlock (MS-NKPU) requests on DHCP port
 67, letting Windows clients boot unattended while on the trusted
 network - without a domain, without WDS, without Windows Server.
 .
 The RSA private key can live in a plain PKCS#8 DER file or behind any
 PKCS#11 module (YubiKey PIV, SoftHSM, OpenSC, TPM2); with a token the
 key never leaves the device. The package ships a systemd unit that can
 prompt for the token PIN at boot via systemd-ask-password, and
 jnkpu-provision-token, which moves a key from a Windows-generated PFX
 onto a YubiKey and writes an offline backup.
 .
 The Recommends cover the token path (pcscd, ykcs11 to talk to a YubiKey,
 yubikey-manager and openssl for provisioning) and the nu-armory relay
 path (bluez, rfkill and python3-dbus/-gi for the BLE bridge that lets the
 dongle open its SE050 ECKey session against the YubiKey). A server that
 only uses the file backend needs none of them.
